    10	STAC Items a client can page through, while `make check` stays a gate a contributor waits for
    11	(under three minutes on CI) and the site's pages build stays within GitHub Pages' limits.
    12	
    13	**Context today (E29 measurements, VPS, 23 Oct 17:40 UTC; CI is about 0.7 of these times).**
    14	Nine tests build the real catalogue (`test_build`, `test_stac`, `test_verify`, `test_manifest`,
    15	`test_mirror`, site snippets); one build writes one STAC Item file per feature of a record with a
    16	period. `make check` today: 2m02 here, 86 s on CI, 18,436 features. With E29's four committed
    17	registers: 2m48 / ~118 s, 25,406 features. With all nine: 8m37 / ~6 min, 177,895 features, 178,056
    18	Item files (193 MB; 35 of 46 s per build in `stac.write_catalog`, Collections indented with tens of
    19	thousands of item links), and the tile test fails: tippecanoe 2.49 writes another feature's string
    20	as `feature_id` for two features (ND #18505, UT #11965 carry BCER well names), the known red of
    21	E18's ruling now reproduced on real data. Pages would publish about 190 MB of STAC and a 150 MB
    22	pmtiles. After E29 merges, the five records carry `inputs`, `period` and `rules.yaml` entries, and
    23	their outlines are one `osd verify --outlines` away.
    24	
    25	**The design the lane must map to.**
    26	1. One real build per test session: a session-scoped fixture builds the catalogue once into a
    27	   temporary directory and the nine tests read it; a test that mutates the build gets its own
    28	   copy. `make check` with all nine registers under three minutes on CI (the PR's check run is the
    29	   proof, its duration stated).
    30	2. STAC writing proportional to the data: Collections written compact (no indentation of item
    31	   link arrays) or Items grouped per Collection in paged link files as the STAC spec allows
    32	   (`rel: next` pages of item links), chosen in the strategy with the client test (OSD-D18 sample
    33	   validation and `make check-full` on the tree); a STAC client (pystac or the QGIS browser,
    34	   stated) lists the Items of North Dakota. Item count and byte size per Collection are printed
    35	   by `osd build` and go in the PR.
    36	3. Tiles: the tippecanoe attribute corruption is reproduced in a fixture test (two features whose
    37	   strings cross), then fixed by a tippecanoe version that is correct (stated and pinned in the
    38	   CI setup) or by writing `feature_id` as a numeric property and keeping strings out of the
    39	   tile attributes (the detail panel reads strings from `records.json` and the outline files,
    40	   not from the tile); the fix is proven by the fixture test and by the real tile of all nine
    41	   registers. The E18 known red is closed in HANDOFF.
    42	4. Outlines for the five records committed under `outlines/` (`osd verify --outlines`, reviewed:
    43	   counts equal the day's `returnCountOnly`), verified with `--outline-inputs` on the branch
    44	   dispatch; the all-record dispatch under 60 minutes, duration stated.
    45	5. Pages: the published site size stated (STAC bytes, pmtiles bytes, records.json bytes) and
    46	   under GitHub Pages' 1 GB site limit with headroom; a phone-width screenshot of North Dakota's
    47	   wells at a town zoom and the detail panel of one well.
    48	
    49	**Acceptance.**
    50	- `make check` on CI under three minutes with all nine registers' outlines committed; the
