docs/program/HANDOFF.md:33:- E18 rulings (23 Oct): `build.py` one line granted (the map layer carries no `osd:period_*`; dates live in the outline files and the STAC Items; tiles stay 60.9 MB). Known red for a later tiles lane: tippecanoe 2.49 wrote wrong attribute values into tiles when the outline features carried the extra date members (publisher_id shown as a date, another feature's raw start), confirmed with tippecanoe-decode; cause not understood, worth testing with `--no-tile-size-limit`/attribute-type flags or a newer tippecanoe before any lane adds properties to the map layer. Sodir dates are M/D/YYYY with optional 12-hour time (rules name the format); NLOG `1800-01-01` is not a placeholder (same shape as 1828 boreholes); NLOG 3D surveys state only a release date and keep the collection period.
