     1	## H2 Verify in shards — CHARTERED · Kernel (hardening) · strategy at lane open · one Codex round
     2	
     3	Authority: owner direction 23 Oct 2026 (levels on the map are real and current; publication on
     4	every merge); OSD-D5 (results on the `verification-results` branch, no bucket, no secret);
     5	OSD-D20 and H1 (dead-link report, issues close on recovery); E23 and E30 (listing readers, 2 s
     6	pause per host); E29 (`--outline-inputs` on ArcGIS layers); `docs/ENGINEERING.md` (hosted
     7	runners, one job class, no infrastructure).
     8	
     9	**Outcome.** An all-record verify dispatch on main finishes in under 25 minutes with the catalogue
    10	of today and stays under 40 minutes when it doubles, and two dispatches never overwrite each other's
    11	results, so every merge can be followed by a verify run without watching a 60-minute ceiling.
    12	
    13	**Context (main ee24f97, 23 Oct).** `.github/workflows/verify.yml` is one job, `timeout-minutes: 60`,
    14	that verifies every record serially (`uv run osd verify --outline-inputs`), then runs `osd status`,
    15	the dead-link report, `make check-full`, force-pushes `build/verification` to
    16	`verification-results` and dispatches `pages.yml`. Measured all-record runs on main: 40 and 43
    17	minutes after E27/E28 (160 records), 56 minutes after E30 (run 39997774390, 176 records counted
    18	after E31 merged during the run; concurrent with run 40002956457); E29's branch run 42.5 minutes
    19	with nine ArcGIS inputs (run 39998588144). Each lane adds listings and inputs. There is no
    20	`concurrency` group: two dispatches on main both force-push `verification-results`, and the one
    21	finishing last wins with whatever earlier results it started from.
    22	
    23	**The design the lane must map to.**
    24	1. `osd verify --shard I/N` selects the records whose stable shard (a hash of the record id, not
    25	   list order, so adding a record moves no other record) is I of N; without `--shard` nothing
    26	   changes. Explicit ids and `--shard` together are an error.
    27	2. On a dispatch with empty `ids`, `verify.yml` runs a matrix of N shards (N stated in the
    28	   strategy from measured per-record times; of the order of 4 to 6) on GitHub-hosted
    29	   `ubuntu-24.04`, each uploading its `build/verification` files as an artifact. One finishing job
    30	   (needs: all shards, runs even when one shard failed) downloads the earlier results, overlays the
    31	   shards' files, then does what the single job does today: `osd status`, dead-link report,
    32	   `make check-full`, store, republish. A shard that times out or fails leaves its records'
    33	   earlier results in place, and the finishing job names the failed shard in the step summary.
    34	   Pull-request runs (changed records only) stay one job.
    35	3. A `concurrency` group for dispatches on main (`cancel-in-progress: false`), so a second
    36	   dispatch queues behind the first and starts from its stored results.
    37	4. A host's 2 s pause holds within a shard; the strategy states how many shards may hit one host at
    38	   once (records of one publisher hash to different shards) and either accepts it with the measured
    39	   counts per host or groups records by origin host in the shard key.
    40	
    41	**Acceptance.**
